<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>living being, animal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.10
			</span></i> (of bees), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				551
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶν ὅ τι περ ἂν μετάσχῃ τοῦ ζῆν
					ζῷον ἂν λέγοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					77b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷα</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				70d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				110e
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. θαλάττιον,
			χερσαῖον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.98S.
			</span></i>; contemptuously, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπως ἡ χώρα τοῦ
				τοιούτου ζῴου καθαρὰ γίγνηται</span> may be free from
			this kind of <i>animal</i> (i.e. beggars), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				936c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. πονηρόν</span>, of women,
				<i><span class="en">
				Secund.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in art,
				<i>figure, image</i>, not necessarily of animals (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῴδιον</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ζῷον δέ οἱ ἐνῆν, ἀνὴρ ἱππεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.88
				</span></i>
			: mostly in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷα ἐς τὴν ἐσθῆτα ἐγγράφειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.203
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.4
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				124
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				148
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				515a
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷα γράψασθαι τὴν ζεῦξιν
				τοῦ Βοσπόρου</span> to have <i>pictures</i> of the
			bridging of the Bosporus painted, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.88
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωγραφέω</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷα ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>sign</i> of the Zodiac, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				2.166
			</span></i>.—The word is post-<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, no generic word used for <i>animal</i> being found till
			after the middle of the fifth cent. B.C. (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώϊον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					13
				</span></i>
			, whence 
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷον</span> by contraction: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span> is found in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.372.42
			</span></i>, al.,<i><span class="en">
				11(2).161
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				76
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.166S.
			</span></i>, and in codd. opt. in the Noun; the Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωός</span> (q.v.) had no <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span>: for the compds. (exc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωγλύφος, ζωγράφος</span>) decisive evidence
			is lacking: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῳάγρια</span> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span> was read by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.407
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
